{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/19037-demonic-form-corruption-aura-questions","id":19037,"title":"[Demonic Form] Corruption Aura Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-27T01:31:33-08:00","id":19037,"title":"[Demonic Form] Corruption Aura Questions","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Corruption Aura<br /> <br /> Sometimes manmade structures and buildings impede proper Infrastructure construction and they must<br /> be destroyed to make room. Sometimes, these buildings cannot just be knocked down or blown up \u2013<br /> though that is an option in many cases. Instead the buildings must be degraded over time. Angels tasked<br /> with destroying these buildings are equipped with means to corrupt and degrade the buildings<br /> fundamental construction. Once weakened, the building can be destroyed with natural occurrences or<br /> just left to finish rotting on its own. Demons use their corrupting essence for a variety of reasons, such<br /> as destroying evidence, disarming enemies, and ruining God-Machine Infrastructure. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System: The demon can activate his aura, which erodes and degrades any kind of <b>non</b>-<b>natural</b> structure<br /> within a <b>five foot aura</b> around him. The demon and his possessions are immune to his own Aura.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Success: Any <b>large structure takes one structural damage every five minutes it is within his Aura</b>. Smaller<br /> items, such as hand-held weapons, portable radios, and cell phones take this damage at a rate of one<br /> structural damage every other round.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The demon can direct his aura to corrupt <b>organic matter </b>as well as <b>non-organic</b>. His<br /> aura wilts plants and flowers, and deals 1B damage every other round to living, and undead creatures<br /> within his aura. </div> </div> </div>1. I assume non-natural structure means non-organic matter ? <br /> <br /> 2. Isn't a five foot radius very small and the overall effect very limited? In the opening discription of the power it says the aura is meant to destroy buildings, but then a 10 foot diameter seems very small when the power is meant to corrode buildings. Also, a demon has to stand around for (5 minutes * 7 structure =) 35 minutes to even errode and degrade a simple wooden door (which has a structure of 7 according to the World of Darkness Rulebook on p. 136).<br /> <br /> The power doesn't seem to do very well what is initially described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T08:54:40-08:00","id":19202,"title":"","content":"1. As formulated, I take it &quot;non-natural&quot; means &quot;artificial AND inorganic&quot;. A cavern with boulders is completely inorganic, for example, but I don't think it would be affected.<br /> 2. Maybe. Use this aura on a couple strategic walls/pillars, though, and the building is toast. It might take a long time, but it's still way faster than getting yourself some explosives and hiding them with the hope no one will find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T19:22:56-08:00","id":19492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/19037-demonic-form-corruption-aura-questions?p=19202#post19202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. As formulated, I take it &quot;non-natural&quot; means &quot;artificial AND inorganic&quot;. A cavern with boulders is completely inorganic, for example, but I don't think it would be affected.<br /> 2. Maybe. Use this aura on a couple strategic walls/pillars, though, and the building is toast. It might take a long time, but it's still way faster than getting yourself some explosives and hiding them with the hope no one will find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, both of these are correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T12:45:10-08:00","id":19860,"title":"","content":"Does it have to be inorganic, or would a structure made from wooden beams fall apart?<br /> <br /> (I'd run it as the latter, no question; interested in the writer opinion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T10:51:27-08:00","id":20249,"title":"","content":"If it's an artificial structure, it'll fall apart, whether the materials are organic or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T11:32:17-08:00","id":20262,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if it had to be inorganic it would be ridiculously restrictive, considering organic means &quot;contains carbon&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}